@startuml
!include theme.puml
title Tuition payment | Durable intent and atomic settlement
autonumber
participant "Student UI\nvia gateway" as UI
participant "Finance API" as API
database finance_db as DB
participant "Provider adapter" as PSP
participant "Finance worker" as W
participant "reconcile_intent\nshared function" as R
UI -> API : POST invoice/{id}/payment-intents
API -> API : Check ownership + pending invoice
group Commit before external I/O
  API -> DB : INSERT intent + unique reference\npartial unique active-intent constraint
  API -> DB : COMMIT
end
API -> PSP : request_to_pay(reference, amount, mobile)
alt Request accepted
  PSP --> API : Accepted / no settlement assertion
else Exception or timeout
  API -> API : Log failure; keep intent pending
end
API --> UI : 201 intent (pending)
loop UI polls 1.5 s while pending; worker polls every 3 s
  alt Worker invocation
    W -> R : reconcile_intent(session, gateway, id)
  else UI status request
    UI -> API : GET payment-intents/{id}
    API -> R : reconcile_intent(session, gateway, id)
  end
  R -> DB : SELECT intent FOR UPDATE
  alt Terminal intent
    R -> R : Return stored state; no duplicate posting
  else Pending intent
    R -> PSP : get_status(reference)
    alt Provider PENDING
      R -> R : Remain pending
    else Provider FAILED
      R -> DB : Set intent failed; COMMIT
    else Provider SUCCESSFUL
      R -> DB : SELECT invoice FOR UPDATE
      group One ACID commit
        R -> DB : Set intent succeeded + invoice paid
        R -> DB : INSERT cash debit + revenue credit\nsame posting_id; equal totals
        R -> DB : INSERT receipt (unique invoice_id)
        R -> DB : COMMIT all settlement changes
      end
    end
  end
end
UI -> API : GET owned invoice receipt
API --> UI : application/pdf
note over API,PSP
Callback body is only a reference hint; provider status is authoritative.
Current gateway blocks unauthenticated callback ingress.
Poller queries status; it does not resubmit a lost MTN request.
Provider call is inside the reconciliation lock lifetime.
end note
@enduml
